{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:stage1-codex-01\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result claims an occurrence rate for the entire 96-station scheduled network but divides the 18 observed occurrences by only the 72 stations retained after screening.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow assigns SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS, rather than SCHEDULED_STATIONS, as the selected result's exposure denominator while labeling the result as applying to the entire scheduled network.\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated scientific task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report defines the target population as all 96 scheduled stations.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected report explicitly uses the 72 retained stations as its denominator while claiming a rate for the entire scheduled network.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The generating workflow directly constructs the selected result with SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS as the denominator.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"DENOMINATOR_LINE = f'Exposure denominator: the {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} stations retained after the signal screen.' + LF\\nSELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The numerator and denominator do form an internally coherent retained-subset rate because the report identifies all 18 occurrences as observed among retained stations; this would falsify the issue if the target and claim were also subset-conditional.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report discloses that no approved protocol change redefined the analysis target.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":17,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"## Protocol status\\nNo protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the mismatch by checking whether the scientific target or selected claim was explicitly conditional on passing the screen. The retained-subset accounting supports 18/72 as a conditional rate, but task.md line 1 and results/report.md lines 4 and 15 instead specify the entire scheduled network, so the attempt failed.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report defines the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations and labels the selected result as applying among those stations.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\\nPlanned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow generates the selected result using the same explicitly conditional population.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"TARGET_LINE = f'Target population: {SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.' + LF\\nACCOUNTING_LINE = f'Planned-unit accounting: {OCCURRENCES} eligible stations with an occurrence, {ELIGIBLE_WITHOUT_OCCURRENCE} eligible stations without an occurrence, and {OUTSIDE_ELIGIBLE} scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.' + LF\\nINPUT_LINE = f'Input table lines including header: {SOURCE_LINE_COUNT}.' + LF\\nRESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"A complete 96-station scheduled network exists, with 24 stations outside the eligible subset, so a complete-domain target would require a different denominator; however, the visible target does not ask that question.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\\nTarget population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\\nPlanned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input explicitly records 24 stations as outside the signal-eligible population and not assessed.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"outside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to find a selected claim requiring the full 96-station network despite using 72 as its denominator. The report mentions the scheduled network for accounting, but its target and selected-result lines expressly condition the analysis on signal eligibility, so the complete-domain denominator mismatch is not demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The task requires a revised occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected report retains all 96 scheduled stations in the exposure denominator and reports 18/96, rather than 18/72.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow constructs both the denominator statement and selected result from SCHEDULED_STATIONS.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"DENOMINATOR_LINE = f'Exposure denominator: all {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations, so the {OMITTED_STATIONS} omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.' + LF\\nSELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The occurrence numerator is observed only among the 72 retained stations, while 24 scheduled stations lack usable observations; this limits interpretation but does not show use of a retained-subset exposure denominator.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen and left without a usable observation: 24\\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report expressly characterizes the resulting complete-network value as a lower bound because omitted stations were unobserved.\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":17,\"end_line\":19,\"quoted_text\":\"## Limitations\\nThe 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the bounded good judgment by locating any selected rate or claim that divided by the 72 retained stations. The selected report instead explicitly divides by all 96 scheduled stations, and its limitations state that no screened-subset rate is reported. The unobserved omitted stations create a separate interpretation limitation, but not the denominator issue in scope.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}"}}
